**Figure 6** and Appendix Figure 9 show that without game-and-role-specific EMA baselines, vanilla REINFORCE may collapse into emitting minimal/invalid reasoning strings after ≈100–200 updates:
- average reasoning response length falls from ≈2,000 characters to nearly zero;
- the authors report general reasoning average dropping from **44% to 40%**;
- with RAE it remains near **1,300–1,500 characters**, and reasoning averages rise **from ≈40% to ≈47%**.
- Figure 9 also reports vanished/noisy gradients without RAE after ≈200 steps and more stable gradients with RAE.
